# Reference: environment variables expected on the host (export before running make targets).
# Workshop VMs usually pre-configure these — verify with: env | grep -E '^(REALM|ACCESS_TOKEN|INSTANCE)='
#
# Required for deploy / collector:
#   REALM              Splunk Observability Cloud realm (e.g. us0)
#   ACCESS_TOKEN       Org ingest access token
#
# Optional (workshop defaults when INSTANCE is set):
#   DEPLOYMENT_ENV     workshop-${INSTANCE}
#   RUM_TOKEN          RUM browser access token (frontend build)
#   RUM_APP_NAME       workshop-${INSTANCE}
#   CLUSTER_NAME       ${INSTANCE}-cluster  (Splunk Infrastructure navigator label; often matches k3d cluster)
#   INSTANCE           workshop instance id
#   K3D_CLUSTER_NAME   optional; if set but missing from k3d, CLUSTER_NAME is used instead
#   REGISTRY           localhost:5111
#   TAG                latest
#   VITE_DEV_PROXY     http://localhost:8080  (local frontend dev only)
